ping into osteoblasts and chondroblasts are derived from the mesoderm. Those developing into odontoblasts are neural crest cells. Those developing into ameloblasts are derived from the ectoderm. (http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=scleroblasts)\")\n22610: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0007001 \"skeletogenic cell\")\n22611: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0007001 obo:CL_0000000)\n22612: \n22613: # Class: obo:CL_0007002 (precementoblast)\n22614: \n22615: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007002 \"Skeletogenic cell that has the potential to develop into a cementoblast.\")\n22616: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0007002 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9114-8737>)\n22617: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_0007002 \"2012-06-15T04:37:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n\n(Showing lines 22598-22617 of 35584. Use offset=22618 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"SubClassOf(obo:CL_0007000 obo:CL_0011026)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0007000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0005176))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0007000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0002077))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0007000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0001763))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0007001 (skeletogenic cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007001 \"Cell that has the potential to form a skeletal cell type (e.g. cells in periosteum, cells in marrow) and produce extracellular matrix (often mineralized) and skeletal tissue (often mineralized).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0007001 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9114-8737>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_0007001 \"2012-06-15T02:51:27Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0007001 \"scleroblast\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0007001 \"Needs logical definition. Should be capable_of skeletal system morphogenesis? or skeletal tissue development? needs to be added to GO. NOTES:a cell type of the early embryo (see also: mesenchymal cells) that will give rise to mineralized connective tissue. Scleroblasts can differentiate into osteoblasts (bone-forming cells), chondroblasts (cartilage-forming cells), odontoblasts (dentin-forming cells), ameloblasts (enamel-forming cells). The mesenchymal cells developing into osteoblasts and chondroblasts are derived from the mesoderm. Those developing into odontoblasts are neural crest cells. Those developing into ameloblasts are derived from the ectoderm. (http://www.copewithcytokines.de/cope.cgi?key=scleroblasts)\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0007001 \"skeletogenic cell\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0007001 obo:CL_0000000)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0007002 (precementoblast)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007002 \"Skeletogenic cell that has the potential to develop into a cementoblast.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0007002 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9114-8737>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_0007002 \"2012-06-15T04:37:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778975595185,"end":1778975595268}},"id":"prt_e333558aa001264Eb1KYEPgwxj","sessionID":"ses_1cccb23aeffeggp6wQdr0yt1hz","messageID":"msg_e333553210014gVrtDPEBeeEuT"}}
