{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778975722464,"sessionID":"ses_1cccb23aeffeggp6wQdr0yt1hz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_3m9kV4H3OST0qH2dC3EbCMk8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Added the requested `hybrid osteochondral skeletal cell` term in PR #<NN>.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+## Summary\n+\n+Added a new Cell Ontology term for issue #3534:\n+\n+- `CL_9900001` hybrid osteochondral skeletal cell\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The issue requested a new term for a murine periosteal skeletal cell that emerges in rib repair callus and displays hybrid osteochondral properties. I used `skeletogenic cell` (`CL_0007001`) as the parent because this is the existing CL term matching the requested skeletal cell parent concept. I added a `part_of` restriction to periosteum (`UBERON_0001434`) and a mouse taxon restriction (`NCBITaxon_10090`) because the cited paper and issue describe the cell in mice.\n+\n+The definition is supported by PMID:30983567 and reflects the reported rib periosteal/callus context and co-expression of cartilage and bone regulators and matrix genes.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Checked for existing related terms using `hybrid osteochondral`, `osteochondral`, `skeletal`, and periosteum-related searches in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Verified parent term selection against existing CL content.\n+- Verified `UBERON_0001434` is already used for periosteum in CL.\n+- Looked up PMID:30983567 via PubMed because `aurelian` was not installed in the environment.\n+- Added issue tracker annotation for obophenotype/cell-ontology#3534.\n+- Added contributor ORCID from the issue.\n+- Added creator and date metadata for the new term.\n+- Ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`; it completed successfully.\n+\n+GitHub Copilot\n*** End Patch"},"ou